      "message": "This loop and the one for the 2D array case below now look pretty similar. Could you factor the loop out, and just handle the glFramebufferTexture2D / glFramebufferTextureLayer() difference below it?\n\nIn fact, could you factor the switch out of TextureView::BindToFramebuffer():\n\n```\n   switch (textarget) {\n        case GL_TEXTURE_2D_ARRAY:\n        case GL_TEXTURE_CUBE_MAP_ARRAY:\n        case GL_TEXTURE_3D:\n            gl.FramebufferTextureLayer(target, attachment, handle, mipLevel, arrayLayer);\n            break;\n        case GL_TEXTURE_CUBE_MAP: {\n            GLenum cubeTexTarget \u003d GL_TEXTURE_CUBE_MAP_POSITIVE_X + arrayLayer;\n            gl.FramebufferTexture2D(target, attachment, cubeTexTarget, handle, mipLevel);\n            break;\n        }\n        default:\n            gl.FramebufferTexture2D(target, attachment, textarget, handle, mipLevel);\n            break;\n```\n\ninto a helper function? It could be on Texture itself, then Texture::ClearTexture() (both renderable and non-renderable cases) and TextureView::BindToFramebuffer() could call that. Then I don\u0027t think you\u0027d need any of the switches in Texture::ClearTexture() at all.",
